   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Direct object pronouns",
     "texto": [
      "To avoid repeating the direct object, use **le** (it, masculine), **la** (it, feminine) or **les** (them): **Je prends le médicament** → **Je le prends**.",
      "Before a vowel or a silent **h**, **le/la** is written **l'**: **J'aime le café** → **Je l'aime**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Where the pronoun goes",
     "texto": [
      "The pronoun goes **before the conjugated verb**: **Je le prends**, **Tu la veux ?** (do you want it?).",
      "If there is an infinitive after, the pronoun goes before the infinitive: **Je veux le voir** (I want to see him/it). You don't say **Je le veux voir**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
